// expect-error: NITPICK-MACRO-007
//
// A MACRO'S REACH IS EXACTLY ITS MODULE (D-124). `shared_macro` is declared in
// `lib/exporter.npk` and marked `pub`, and this still cannot invoke it: `pub`
// governs what a module EXPORTS, and a macro is not exported at all.
//
// The reason is hygiene. An identifier in a macro body resolves where the macro
// was WRITTEN (D-057), so an invocation that crossed a module boundary would leave
// the defining scope and the landing scope in different modules — and every later
// pass that walks a declaration would have to carry a second scope alongside the
// one it is in, for a form nothing writes. Not one of the prototype's twenty-five
// macro declarations is `pub`.
//
// ITS OWN CODE, NOT "NAMES NO MACRO". The name is real and the mistake is about
// reach, and only that version of the sentence tells the reader what to change.
mod:cross_module;

use "./lib/exporter.npk".*;

#shared_macro();

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) {
    int32:a = raw anchor();
    exit 0i32;
};
